Subject: [PATCH] mocking: decode the child wait status before exiting

os.system returns a wait status. Passing it directly to sys.exit loses a
normal child failure (for example, exit 7 becomes exit 0). Keep the upstream
wrapper and decode its result using the standard library.

Upstream: https://codeberg.org/DylanVanAssche/libssc
Base: 54dd13e36d65c21263cf5b0f4a70c230a77b26bc
License: GPL-3.0-or-later, as in mocking/ssc_server/ssc-server.in.
---
diff --git a/mocking/ssc_server/ssc-server.in b/mocking/ssc_server/ssc-server.in
index 07a973d..ec3779b 100755
--- a/mocking/ssc_server/ssc-server.in
+++ b/mocking/ssc_server/ssc-server.in
@@ -328,7 +328,7 @@ if __name__ == '__main__':
             p.start()
 
         code = ERROR_OK
-        code = os.system(args.test)
+        code = os.waitstatus_to_exitcode(os.system(args.test))
         if code != 0:
             print(f'❌ Test {args.test} finished with exit code {code}')
 
